## 10. The first unproved theorem, exactly

As required: the strongest verified reductions are preserved and RH is not
claimed.  The first unproved statement on the localized route is

> **`e₂(G_H) ≤ E_prime,loc(T, H)` with `E_prime,loc(T, H) = o(L⁶)` for some
> `H = o(L²)`** — a bounded-height (short-interval) prime-side exterior-area
> bound.

There is no Lean declaration for it in this repository (it is not stated as a
`sorry`ed lemma, by design), and per §8 it is not derivable from the companion's
present inputs.  Even granted it, §7 shows a second obligation is now equally
binding:

> an **`α`-uniform** window energy bound `Bφ(α, L) ≤ C_b L²`, i.e. control of the
> twisted taper masses `taperMass(φ,α)`, `derivMass(φ,α)` that does not degrade
> like `e^{αL/2}` — the hypothesis of `offset_le_of_quadratic_norm_bound`.

Both are strictly weaker than RH, and both are open here.

## 11. Verdict on the localization proposal

* The structural diagnosis was right: the global `e₂` lane is dead for a reason
  no constant can repair (G5), and localization is the correct response.
* The architectural steps all go through, and are now proved rather than
  assumed: multiplicity lift (no `M`), compression functoriality, hot/cold exact
  reopening with a universal property, anchored minors (tight), local transport
  with window-size constants, and real Schur theorems.
* The **arithmetic prediction did not survive contact with the source vectors**.
  The predicted `(log T)⁴` local budget rested on a linear per-vector trace bound
  that is provably false; the true `L²` energy scale puts the localized budget at
  `L⁶`, precisely the order of the floor.  Localization converts a power-of-`T`
  failure into a *critical* constant-order failure.  That is real progress, and
  it is still not a proof.
